AI COMMAND CENTER — ROADMAP
================================================================

PHASE 1 — FOUNDATION .................................. DONE (v0.3.0)
    FastAPI + SQLite (aiosqlite, async, migration-managed),
    modular boundaries (provider, model router, agent, team,
    workspace, tools, research, git, security, observability),
    env config, JSON structured logging, unified errors,
    health checks, schema versioning, encrypted credential vault.

PHASE 2 — PREMIUM CHAT ................................ DONE (v0.3.0)
    Real SSE streaming chat against Ollama; history, search,
    rename, delete, archive, pin, favorites; stop, retry,
    regenerate; markdown + GFM; syntax-highlighted code w/ copy;
    model selector; system prompt + custom instructions; exact/
    estimated token labels; context meter; error states; auto-
    titles from the local model. Zero simulated responses.

PHASE 3 — MODEL CENTER + TOKEN/COST SYSTEM ............ DONE (v0.3.0)
    Live Ollama discovery, categories, search/filter/sort,
    favorites, recently used, selection, speed tests, safe
    pull/delete. Per-model token/cost ledger. Strict €0
    CostGuard (FREE_ONLY, MAX_SPEND, pre-network blocking,
    no paid fallback) — tested against bypass attempts.

PHASE 4 — AGENT MODE + PROJECTS ....................... DONE (v0.8.0)
    - Tool-calling agent engine over SSE (fs_list/read/write/edit,
      shell_run, later web_search/web_fetch/memory_*) with
      max-steps, circuit breaker, cooperative stop
    - Security gateway: capability check → arg validation →
      HUMAN APPROVAL (10 min, exact diff preview) → sandboxed
      execution → audit row (executions + agent_steps/approvals)
    - Projects: slug-deduped sandboxed workspaces, archive-only

PHASE 5 — TEAM MODE (FLAGSHIP) ........................ DONE (v0.8.0)
    - Planner → executor → reviewer pipelines of 2–4 models
    - Executor turns are real agent runs (same gateway/audit)
    - VERDICT parsing with exactly one revision; VRAM-serial locals
    - Compare Mode shipped alongside: 2–4 models side-by-side,
      queued-vs-parallel honesty, per-slot CostGuard isolation

PHASE 6 — RESEARCH MODE ............................... DONE (v0.8.0)
    - Web-grounded answers with numbered [n] citations
    - SSRF-guarded fetch (private/loopback blocked, redirect
      re-validation, hard size caps, honest truncation flags)
    - Failed sources are dropped and said so; no grounding →
      the run fails instead of hallucinating
    - Same web layer powers the agent's web tools (READ-tier)

PHASE 7 — GIT / GITHUB INTEGRATION .................... DONE (v0.9.0)
    - Status, diff (capped), log, branch create+switch, commit,
      push (+set-upstream), remote add — inside the workspace,
      argv-subprocess (no shell), path containment, git:operate
      capability (off by default), every op audited
    - GitHub REST: user, repos, create-private-repo; PAT vault-
      encrypted, delivered via GIT_ASKPASS, never in argv/logs,
      only ever to github.com
    - Destructive ops (reset --hard, force-push, clean) excluded
      by design

PHASE 8 — MEMORY & SKILLS ............................. DONE (v0.10.0)
    - Persistent memories (V5 migration, user CRUD in Settings,
      agent memory_search/save/forget tools; saves approval-gated,
      provenance source="agent:<run_id>")
    - AGENT.md standing instructions chained workspace→project
      into every run's prompt

PHASE 9 — WINDOWS DISTRIBUTION ........................ DONE (v0.11.0)
    - PyInstaller onedir EXE (SPA bundled), pywebview native
      window with browser fallback, portable data dir beside the
      EXE (%LOCALAPPDATA% fallback), deterministic --smoke mode
    - Inno Setup installer + tag-triggered GitHub Actions release
      (full test suite gates the build)

PHASE 10 — FINAL POLISH ............................... DONE (v0.12.0)
    - Command palette (Ctrl+K) with fuzzy-ranked actions, chats
      and models; full keyboard navigation
    - Global shortcuts (Ctrl+B / Ctrl+. / Ctrl+, / Ctrl+Alt+N /
      Ctrl+/ help) + shortcuts reference cards
    - Sidebar date grouping, chat day separators, jump-to-latest,
      message timestamps, focus/selection/reduced-motion polish

RULES (kept): no fake features — every boundary is implemented;
€0 protection never regressed; schema evolved only via new
migrations (V1–V5); no silent provider switching.
